## GS Global Corp. financial statements, 6 years: Back to a profit in 2021 after a net loss of KRW 82.1bn in 2020

The consolidated financial statements in the 2020–2025 annual reports that GS Global Corp. (001250) filed with Korea's DART electronic disclosure system, laid out by year. Figures from the 2026 third-quarter report cover a different period and are shown separately. **Every figure below is taken as filed in the DART submissions; there is no interpretation or outlook.** Amounts are in Korean won (KRW; bn = billion, tn = trillion).

### 1. Income statement — the sign of net income changed in 2021

| Fiscal year | Revenue | Revenue change | Operating income | Op. income change | Operating margin | Net income |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 2.82tn | — | 32.3bn | — | 1.1% | −82.1bn |
| 2021 | 3.85tn | +36.73% | 38.8bn | +20.27% | 1.0% | 22.0bn |
| 2022 | 5.07tn | +31.75% | 70.5bn | +81.40% | 1.4% | 68.1bn |
| 2023 | 3.92tn | −22.77% | 76.5bn | +8.59% | 1.9% | 26.1bn |
| 2024 | 4.07tn | +3.83% | 77.9bn | +1.78% | 1.9% | 56.1bn |
| 2025 | 4.11tn | +1.05% | 52.3bn | −32.84% | 1.3% | 13.9bn |

Revenue was largest in 2022 at KRW 5.07tn and smallest in 2020 at KRW 2.82tn among the six years. It fell from the previous year once: 2023 (−22.77%).

Operating income was largest in 2024 at KRW 77.9bn and smallest in 2020 at KRW 32.3bn. The operating margin was highest in 2023 at 1.9%.

**Net income was largest in 2022 at KRW 68.1bn and smallest in 2020 at KRW −82.1bn.**

### 2. Financial position — equity became 1.91x

| Fiscal year | Total assets | Total equity | Debt ratio | Current ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 956.8bn | 299.0bn | 220.0% | 103.8% |
| 2021 | 1.44tn | 342.5bn | 321.2% | 112.1% |
| 2022 | 1.42tn | 406.7bn | 249.0% | 125.0% |
| 2023 | 1.40tn | 448.0bn | 212.8% | 125.7% |
| 2024 | 1.44tn | 567.1bn | 153.9% | 140.7% |
| 2025 | 1.45tn | 570.4bn | 154.6% | 146.2% |

The debt ratio was highest in 2021 at 321.2% and lowest in 2024 at 153.9%.

Over the same period total assets went from KRW 956.8bn to KRW 1.45tn (1.52x), and **total equity went from KRW 299.0bn to KRW 570.4bn and became 1.91x.**

The current ratio was above 100% in all six years, ranging from 103.8% to 146.2%.

